From 86bca5db90a5531ca9da7ceec9b42ab91a01e8cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:27:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/32] feat(spec): scheduler-side hidden-state dump for MTP
 draft-head training

Adds an env-gated writer that captures, from inside the scheduler process, the
exact tensors the Qwen4-Exp MTP consumes and produces:

  target channel  Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration.forward publishes the hc
                  hidden (hc_count*hidden = 10240) that eagle_worker_v2 hands to
                  the draft; dumped with input_ids and positions per extend
                  forward (EXTEND | MIXED | SPLIT_PREFILL only -- is_extend()
                  alone would also catch TARGET_VERIFY).
  gate channel    Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP.forward, captured BEFORE the
                  LogitsProcessor and _set_hc_logits_hidden_states slice rows,
                  so it holds SGLang own MTP output at every prefill position.
                  That is the reference for the torch re-implementation
                  equivalence gate.

The supported --return-hidden-states path is not usable at this scale:
_append_prefill_hidden_states does .cpu().clone().tolist() per request and ships
Python floats over ZMQ, which is ~42M floats for one 4096-token prefill. The
writer does a pinned D2H copy and a raw sequential write on a background thread.

Entirely inert unless SGLANG_MTP_HIDDEN_DUMP_DIR is set; the gate channel needs
SGLANG_MTP_HIDDEN_DUMP_GATE=1 as well.
